**Disposition:** **PASS at the stated proof-only full-core/no-macroscopic-container Type-II scope.**  
**LEVEL I STATUS:** **STILL OPEN. C-II REMAINS OPEN.**

The candidate raises the parent exclusion from `1.8436` to `1.84362`.  The final
outer-energy contradiction is not the dangerous part: it has more than `0.004D` slack.
The audit therefore concentrates on the only new structural step, the enlarged
phase-localization box

\[
h<0.00028,
\qquad
W<1.912606,
\qquad
U,V<0.525.
\]

The remaining modules are the same ones independently audited for the `1.8436`
theorem, with strictly weaker numerical conclusions.

---

## 1. Residual localization really extends to `h<0.00028`

At the adverse endpoint

\[
t=1.84362,
\qquad h=0.00028,
\qquad x=0,
\]

the exact certificate evaluates the parent survivor-capacity boundary and obtains

\[
F(A)-\delta>2.3269\times10^{-5}.
\]

The parent derivative estimates remain strict on the enlarged box:

\[
Q_h<-2.5,
\qquad
Q_x<-2.7.
\]

The detour ceiling remains below `0.052`, so none of the denominator bounds used in
the derivative proof changes sign.  Thus increasing either residual variable can only
make survival harder, and every survivor with `t<=1.84362` satisfies

\[
0\le h<0.00028-o(1).
\]

**Verdict:** PASS.

