## 6. The one-variable main capacity has no missed interior maximum

After the adverse replacement, write the one-variable capacity as `G(C)`.  The exact
algebra used by the parent theorem gives

\[
G''(C)<-2
\]

throughout the main interval.  The certificate checks the load-bearing polynomial at
the lower endpoint; its left side is increasing with `C`, so this controls the whole
interval.

At

\[
c_*=0.931922
\]

the tangent parabola bound gives

\[
\max G
\le G(c_*)+{G'(c_*)^2\over4}
<0.9068995-1.47\times10^{-5}.
\]

The generic center capacity separately excludes `C>=1.044`, and the certificate also
checks `C<=0.525` is impossible.  Thus all center regimes are covered.

Therefore

\[
\boxed{U,V<0.525-o(1)}
\]

is valid.

**Verdict:** PASS.

