## 8. Pair weight and common-center loss are normalized correctly

From

\[
z_i\le M_i+P_i+o(1),
\]

the two leaf bounds give

\[
P_U,P_V>0.7100-0.525-o(1)=0.185-o(1).
\]

For the common-center step, the candidate substitutes

\[
W<1.912606,
\quad E_{dom}>0.9068995,
\quad U<0.525
\]

into

\[
B_{bad}
\le{2[C(W-C)-E_{dom}]\over C-U}+o(1).
\]

The denominator is positive: generic center capacity gives `C>0.525`, and the exact
certificate checks

\[
0.525(1.912606-0.525)<0.9068995.
\]

Replacing `W,E,U` by the displayed adverse bounds can only increase the quotient.  The
claim `B_bad<0.036` reduces to a quadratic with positive leading coefficient and exact
discriminant

\[
<-0.00106<0.
\]

Thus even charging the entire bad weight to one leaf leaves

\[
G_U,G_V>0.149-o(1).
\]

No weighted-to-unweighted conversion is used.

**Verdict:** PASS.

