## 9. The final cross-leaf energy ledger inherits the parent hostile audit unchanged

Every good leaf train crosses more than half of the same finite center family.  Hence
every good U/V pair shares a center neighbor.  Triangle-freeness of the stopped-train
crossing graph forces that pair to be noncrossing.  The hostile-audited endpoint theorem
then gives

\[
e_\tau+e_\sigma\ge2-\sqrt3-o(1).
\]

Weighted complete-product averaging gives

\[
E_U+E_V
\ge(2-\sqrt3)\min(G_U,G_V)-o(1)
>(2-\sqrt3)(0.149)-o(1).
\]

This leaf terminal energy is a submeasure of the two leaf selected outer-edge
populations.  The center one-well term `f(z_C)` is supported on the disjoint center
phase window, so the two payments add without double counting.

The exact certificate proves

\[
(2-\sqrt3)(0.149)+f(0.7100)
>{R_{1.84362}\over2}+0.00434.
\]

This is a macroscopic contradiction and absorbs all source-limit/window-limit errors.

**Verdict:** PASS.

