## Final disposition

All new obligations introduced by moving the endpoint from `1.8436` to `1.84362` pass:

- residual localization to `h<0.00028`;
- larger-leaf localization to `U,V<0.525`;
- retained total mass `z>2.2195`;
- phasewise retained mass `z_i>0.7100`;
- total bad common-center pair weight `<0.036`;
- final disjoint outer-energy contradiction with margin `>0.00434`.

Therefore the candidate proof-only full-core Type-II strengthening

\[
\boxed{\liminf (q-k)/D\ge1.84362}
\]

is certified at its stated scope.

C-II and Level I remain open.
